@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mw-il32-nouns`

-- Minimum Wage Law 5747-1987, s 3: which pay counts towards the minimum wage.

§ `Section 3 — the pay that is taken into account`

§§ `Which kinds of component count`

-- s 3(a): the pay taken into account for s 2 is the pay the employer pays the employee for a regular
-- working day as customary at the workplace. s 3(b) lists what counts: (1) a basic or combined wage;
-- (2) a cost-of-living supplement, if not included in the combined wage; (3) a fixed supplement paid to
-- the employee by reason of his work. The proviso then says what is "not taken into account": a family
-- supplement, a seniority supplement, a supplement for shift work, a measured, agreed, fixed or group
-- premium, a thirteenth salary, annual grants, and a refund of expenses including board, per diem and
-- travel. The proviso governs: a fixed supplement that is also, say, a seniority supplement is a
-- seniority supplement (the caller classifies it so). A component the text neither lists nor excludes
-- is fork F3.
-- src:33 | (א) השכר שיובא בחשבון לענין סעיף 2 יהיה שכר העבודה שמשלם מעסיק לעובדו בעד יום עבודה רגיל כנהוג במקום עבודתו.
-- src:34 | (ב) לענין סעיף קטן (א) יבואו בחשבון רכיבי השכר הבאים:
-- src:35 | (1) שכר יסוד או שכר משולב;
-- src:36 | (2) תוספת יוקר אם איננה כלולה בשכר המשולב;
-- src:37 | (3) תוספת קבועה המשתלמת לעובד עקב עבודתו,
-- src:40 | ואולם לא יובאו בחשבון תוספת משפחה, תוספת ותק, תוספת בשל עבודה במשמרות, פרמיה מדודה, מוסכמת, קבועה או קבוצתית, משכורת י״ג, מענקים על בסיס שנתי, והחזר הוצאות לרבות הוצאות כלכלה, אש״ל ונסיעות שמשלם המעסיק.
@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(b)(1)-(3) and proviso (source lines 35-37, 40)
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of pay component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3(b) counts the kind` `the kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a basic wage or a combined wage`                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a cost-of-living supplement not included in a combined wage` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a fixed supplement paid by reason of the work`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a family supplement`                                         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a seniority supplement`                                      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a supplement for shift work`                                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a measured, agreed, fixed or group premium`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a thirteenth salary`                                         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an annual grant`                                             THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a refund of expenses, including board, per diem and travel`  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a component the text does not name`                          THEN FALSE

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(b) (source lines 34-40); fork F3
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of pay component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the kind is one the text neither lists nor excludes` `the kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a component the text does not name` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(b)(1) and (2) (source lines 35-36)
GIVEN `the components` IS A LIST OF `A pay component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the pay has a basic or combined wage` `the components` MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD c's `kind` EQUALS `a basic wage or a combined wage`) `the components`

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(b)(2) (source line 36)
GIVEN `the components` IS A LIST OF `A pay component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the pay has a cost-of-living supplement` `the components` MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD c's `kind` EQUALS `a cost-of-living supplement not included in a combined wage`) `the components`

§§ `The pay that counts: sections 3(a), (b) and (d)`

-- s 3(d): "if the employee's wage was not payable by the components listed in subsection (b)(1) and
-- (2), or by some of them, the wage for s 3(a) shall be calculated by the regular wage without
-- additions". Which pay structures that reaches is fork F2:
--   (P) only a pay with neither a basic or combined wage nor a cost-of-living supplement;
--   (L) a pay lacking either of them (so that a pay with a basic wage and no separate cost-of-living
--       supplement, the usual case of a combined wage, would count its basic wage alone).
-- They give different amounts for a pay with a basic wage and a fixed supplement; default: decline.
-- src:42 | (ד) לא היה שכרו של עובד משתלם לפי הרכיבים המנויים בסעיף קטן (ב)(1) ו־(2), או לפי חלק מהם, יחושב השכר לענין סעיף קטן (א) לפי שכר העבודה הרגיל ללא תוספות.
@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(d) (source line 42); fork F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the pay`        IS A `Pay for a regular working day`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the regular pay without additions that section 3(d) uses, from` `the pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the pay`'s `the regular pay without additions`
    WHEN JUST x THEN x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "section 3(d) calculates the pay by the regular wage without additions, and none was given"

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(b) (source lines 34-40); fork F3
GIVEN `unlisted components count` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the component`             IS A `A pay component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a component counts where unlisted ones count:` `unlisted components count` `the component` MEANS
    (`section 3(b) counts the kind` (`the component`'s `kind`))
    OR (`unlisted components count` AND `the kind is one the text neither lists nor excludes` (`the component`'s `kind`))

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(a), (b), (d) (source lines 33-37, 40, 42)
GIVEN `the pay`                   IS A `Pay for a regular working day`
      `section 3(d) applies`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `unlisted components count` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pay that counts for` `the pay` `where` `section 3(d) applies` `and` `unlisted components count` MEANS
    IF   `section 3(d) applies`
    THEN `the regular pay without additions that section 3(d) uses, from` `the pay`
    ELSE sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `amount`) (filter (GIVEN c YIELD `a component counts where unlisted ones count:` `unlisted components count` c) (`the pay`'s `components`)))

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(d) (source line 42); fork F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the pay`    IS A `Pay for a regular working day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3(d) applies under reading P` `the pay` MEANS
    (NOT (`the pay has a basic or combined wage` (`the pay`'s `components`))) AND (NOT (`the pay has a cost-of-living supplement` (`the pay`'s `components`)))

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(d) (source line 42); fork F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the pay`    IS A `Pay for a regular working day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3(d) applies under reading L` `the pay` MEANS
    (NOT (`the pay has a basic or combined wage` (`the pay`'s `components`))) OR (NOT (`the pay has a cost-of-living supplement` (`the pay`'s `components`)))

§§ `The readings the switches allow (forks F2 and F3)`

-- Each switch allows one reading, or, at its default, both. The amount that counts under every
-- allowed combination is the list below. Where they all agree the amount is that one; where they do
-- not, the amount declines by name. A comparison with the minimum asks a narrower question, so
-- it answers wherever every allowed combination lands on the same side of the minimum.
@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(d); fork F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the pay`      IS A `Pay for a regular working day`
      `the reading`  IS A `When section 3(d) applies`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`the ways section 3(d) may apply to` `the pay` `read` `the reading` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reading`
    WHEN `only when the pay has neither a basic or combined wage nor a cost-of-living supplement` THEN LIST (`section 3(d) applies under reading P` `the pay`)
    WHEN `when the pay lacks either of them`                                                       THEN LIST (`section 3(d) applies under reading L` `the pay`)
    WHEN `decline where the readings differ`                                                       THEN LIST (`section 3(d) applies under reading P` `the pay`), (`section 3(d) applies under reading L` `the pay`)

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(b); fork F3; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the reading`  IS A `Whether an unlisted component counts`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`the ways unlisted components may count under` `the reading` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reading`
    WHEN `it counts`                         THEN LIST TRUE
    WHEN `it does not count`                 THEN LIST FALSE
    WHEN `decline where the readings differ` THEN LIST TRUE, FALSE

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(a), (b), (d); forks F2 and F3
GIVEN `the pay`        IS A `Pay for a regular working day`
      `the d reading`  IS A `When section 3(d) applies`
      `the u reading`  IS A `Whether an unlisted component counts`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the amounts that may count for` `the pay` `read` `the d reading` `and` `the u reading` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN u YIELD map (GIVEN d YIELD `the pay that counts for` `the pay` `where` d `and` u) (`the ways section 3(d) may apply to` `the pay` `read` `the d reading`))
                (`the ways unlisted components may count under` `the u reading`))

@ref Minimum Wage Law s 3(a), (b), (d); forks F2 and F3; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the pay`        IS A `Pay for a regular working day`
      `the d reading`  IS A `When section 3(d) applies`
      `the u reading`  IS A `Whether an unlisted component counts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pay that counts for` `the pay` `read` `the d reading` `and` `the u reading` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amounts that may count for` `the pay` `read` `the d reading` `and` `the u reading`
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN
        IF   all (GIVEN y YIELD y EQUALS x) xs
        THEN x
        ELSE REFUSE "sections 3(b) and 3(d) do not decide which pay counts here: the allowed readings (whether section 3(d) applies, whether an unlisted component counts) give different amounts"
    WHEN EMPTY THEN REFUSE "no pay was given"

§§ `Whether the pay meets the minimum`

-- s 2(a): the pay "shall not be less than" the minimum wage. Equal meets it ("לא יפחת"). A pay for a
-- regular working day is compared with a figure of the same period; the caller supplies the minimum
-- for that period (monthly for a monthly wage, the daily figure for a daily one).
@ref Minimum Wage Law s 2(a) (source line 28), s 3(a) (source line 33)
GIVEN `the pay`        IS A `Pay for a regular working day`
      `the d reading`  IS A `When section 3(d) applies`
      `the u reading`  IS A `Whether an unlisted component counts`
      `the minimum wage for the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the pay meets the minimum wage:` `the pay` `read` `the d reading` `and` `the u reading` `against` `the minimum wage for the period` MEANS
    BRANCH IF all (GIVEN y YIELD y AT LEAST `the minimum wage for the period`) (`the amounts that may count for` `the pay` `read` `the d reading` `and` `the u reading`) THEN TRUE
           IF all (GIVEN y YIELD y LESS THAN `the minimum wage for the period`) (`the amounts that may count for` `the pay` `read` `the d reading` `and` `the u reading`) THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "sections 3(b) and 3(d) do not decide whether this pay meets the minimum: the allowed readings put it on different sides of the minimum"
